## Implementation Plan (ordered)

| Step | Change | Blocking? | Effort |
|------|--------|-----------|--------|
| 1 | Create `jurkatFCBsmall` (5k-cell subsample) as in-package dataset | Yes | Low |
| 2 | Rewrite vignette to run on `jurkatFCBsmall` with `eval = TRUE` throughout; remove `vignettes/data/` | Yes | Medium |
| 3 | Register `jurkatFCB` on ExperimentHub (or document as future work) | Yes (size) | High |
| 4 | Add `biocViews` to DESCRIPTION | Yes | Low |
| 5 | Create `NEWS.md` | Yes | Low |
| 6 | Add `URL`/`BugReports` to DESCRIPTION | Yes | Low |
| 7 | Fix `T` → `TRUE` / `F` → `FALSE` (3 instances) | No | Low |
| 8 | Create `inst/CITATION` | No | Low |
| 9 | Replace `pracma::findintervals` with `findInterval` | No | Low |
| 10 | Add `BiocStyle` to vignette | No | Low |
| 11 | Run `BiocCheck` and address remaining warnings | No | Medium |

**Note on step 3 (ExperimentHub):** Registering a dataset on ExperimentHub is a separate, multi-step process involving a companion metadata package (`DebarcodeRData`) and a Bioconductor PR. If this is not ready before submission, an acceptable interim approach is to submit with only `jurkatFCBsmall` in the package and note in the vignette that the full dataset will be submitted to ExperimentHub. The package will still pass size limits with just `jurkatFCBsmall` (<1 MB total).

Steps 1–2 and 4–6 are the critical path. Steps 7–11 are straightforward polish. Step 3 can be deferred.

